**Declared actions.** This step MUST do exactly these, and the worker base prompt says what each verb obliges:
- `ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.PlanViewTests`

**How to implement.** The Plan view, its own surface and the flow strip's Plan step between Unknowns and Fit (001 §O 'a left flow strip: Items → Setups → Experiments → Data → Unknowns → Plan → Fit → Results → Publish'; 'Plan view: the recoverability report (rank, confounded combinations, CRB per target)'; 'Automation: … `PlanRunButton`'; the S14.2 brief; .spec-md §3.22: a step appears when it works; .spec-md §10.1 discoverability: the plan view is a flow-strip step, §10.5 opposing pairs on one row). The Plan step is the Inverse constructor's alone, as the study's steps are (step 414); it is a step of the kit window, not a window, so no `WindowFit.keepOnScreen` call is added, and it joins `ScrollExtentTests` (.spec-md §4 'UI'). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S14.2. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: `ConstructorFlowStep` (steps 238, 242, 323, 414-418) gains `PlanFlowStep` between `UnknownsFlowStep` and `FitFlowStep`, its `caption` `Plan` and its `flowUiId` `flowPlanStep`; `all` lists Items, Setups, Experiments, Data, Unknowns, Plan, Fit, Results and Publish, and `stepsOf ForwardConstructor` answers `all` without Data and the study's steps, Plan among them. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`, a group after the Unknowns step's under `// --- The study's Plan step (PlanView). ---`, each with a one-line doc: `flowPlanStep` (`"FlowPlanStep"`), `planPanel` (`"PlanPanel"`), `planRunButton` (`"PlanRunButton"`, 001 §O), `planCriterionDeterminantChoice` (`"PlanCriterionDeterminantChoice"`), `planCriterionTraceChoice` (`"PlanCriterionTraceChoice"`), `planProgressBar` (`"PlanProgressBar"`), `planProgressText` (`"PlanProgressText"`), `planCancelButton` (`"PlanCancelButton"`), `planErrorText` (`"PlanErrorText"`), `planFindingsList` (`"PlanFindingsList"`), `planRankText` (`"PlanRankText"`), `planConfoundedList` (`"PlanConfoundedList"`), `planBoundsGrid` (`"PlanBoundsGrid"`) and `planInstrumentList` (`"PlanInstrumentList"`). `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs`: `planMaterialChoice (version : MaterialVersionId)` is `PlanMaterial_<the GUID>_v<n>`. (3) New `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/PlanView.fs`, `module OpticalConstructor.Ui.PlanView`, compiled directly after `StudyUnknownsView.fs` (step 414) and before `StudyFitView.fs`: one `<Compile>` line, no comment; its module doc one to three lines citing 001 §O and spec 0050 S14.2. `planView (model : TableAndElementRotationModel) (dispatch : TableAndElementRotationMsg -> unit) : IView`: a `ScrollViewer` scrolling both ways around a vertical `StackPanel` carrying `planPanel`, margin 8, holding `StudyUnknownsView.studyBarView` (step 414) and, for the chosen study, in order: (a) `Material:` and one box per `model.planMaterials` carrying `planMaterialChoice` and its name and version, sending `SetPlanMaterial`, the chosen one an `actionButton` on `positiveBackground` and the others `MaterialsWindowView.verbButton`s (step 241's chosen-option look), or the line `The study opens no crystal material: open one in Unknowns.`; (b) `Rank candidates by:` and the two boxes of `PlanCriterion.text` (`planCriterionDeterminantChoice`, `planCriterionTraceChoice`) sending `SetPlanCriterion`, the chosen one on `positiveBackground`; (c) one horizontal `StackPanel` of `Run plan` (`planRunButton`, an `actionButton` on `positiveBackground`, sending `StudyPlan (RunPlan { study; material = <planMaterialOpt>; criterion })`, present with a material and disabled while the job runs) and, while it runs, with a right margin as the gap, `Cancel` (`planCancelButton`, on `negativeBackground`, sending `StudyPlan CancelPlan`); while it runs a determinate `ProgressBar` carrying `planProgressBar` at the progress's `fraction` and `planJob.job.progressText` in a `TextBlock` carrying `planProgressText` (`JobRunner.fs:JobModel`): progress per candidate, one click with Cancel (.spec-md §10.2, §10.3); (d) `planJob.errorOpt`'s `describe` in a wrapping `TextBlock` carrying `planErrorText`, in `MaterialsWindowView.messageColor`; (e) for `model.planReportOpt`: `What the kit can recover:` and a vertical `StackPanel` carrying `planFindingsList`, one wrapping line per structural finding's `text` (step 469), then `<label>: no principal axis lies on its normal, so the plan places no candidate on it.` per unplaced plate and `The kit has no Mueller polarimeter, so the plan has no candidate.` without one; a `TextBlock` carrying `planRankText`, `Rank <r> of <n> from what the kit holds; condition <κ, two decimals>.` or, below full rank, `Rank <r> of <n> from what the kit holds: <n − r> combination(s) confounded.`; a vertical `StackPanel` carrying `planConfoundedList`, one line per confounded direction's `text` over the report's targets and `Weakest: <its text>` for the weakest; a `Grid` carrying `planBoundsGrid`, four `Auto` columns `Target`, `Value`, `σ` and `σ / value`, a semi-bold header and one row per baseline bound (the value the target's axis reads in `nominal`, invariant culture, `G6`), or the line `No bound yet: what the kit holds leaves a combination confounded.`; and `Instrument states:` with a vertical `StackPanel` carrying `planInstrumentList`, one line per instrument finding's `text` (step 483). The ranked candidates are step 491's. (4) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitWindowView.fs`: `PlanFlowStep` shows `PlanView.planView model dispatch` keyed `plan`. Tests. `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/TestAppScope.fs` gains `planKitOver (context : AppContext) (owner : FolderName) : TableAndElementRotationModel` and `planKitIn (owner : FolderName) : TableAndElementRotationModel`, `planKitOver (freshAppContext owner) owner`, each with a one-line doc citing spec 0050 S14.2, the one plan fixture of the UI suite, built as `studyKitIn` builds its kit (step 414): over `context` and a kit from `openedKitIn owner`, a user uniaxial crystal material (n_o 1.544, n_e 1.553, g11 3.0e-5, g33 −1.0e-5, step 355's probe) saved through the context's material store, a plate sample of it, 0.5 mm, `PrimaryAxes`, `EmitBoth`, built as `PlannerInputsTests` builds QZ-Z and saved through the context's sample store, and the items Laser (`PresetIds.heNe633`), QZ-Z (that sample) and Polarimeter (`ItemModelIds.muellerPolarimeterModelId`) recorded through the kit's library (`recordItem`, step 219); the kit is closed, opened again through `KitOpening.openKitAt` and loaded into an Inverse model, the Polarimeter assigned to `det` (`AssignSlot`, step 263), and the study QZ created, the material opened and g11 and g33 freed (`StudyCommand`, `SetOpenedMaterialParameter`, steps 366, 409) at their values within ±50 %. New `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/PlanViewTests.fs`, `module PlanViewTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests`, appended at the end of the compile list with no comment, its screens mounted as `KitWindowTests` mounts `kitWindowView` (step 242). Without a trait: `the plan view UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`: the fourteen fixed ids' texts and `planMaterialChoice` of a test-local version; `the Plan step shows a plan's findings, rank, confounded combinations, bounds and instrument choices`: over `planKitIn` with a plan run through `PlanJobHost.posting` as `PlanJobTests` drives it (step 487), on `PlanFlowStep`, `planFindingsList` holds the off-axis-cut finding, `planRankText` reads `Rank 0 of 2 from what the kit holds: 2 combination(s) confounded.`, `planBoundsGrid` is absent and the no-bound line shown, and `planInstrumentList` holds no line. With trait `ui-smoke`: `pressing Run plan starts one plan through the shell's host, and Cancel cancels it`: with the shell's `planRuns` a test-local host recording its jobs and its cancel, pressing `flowPlanStep` and `planRunButton` records one job and shows `planProgressBar` and `planCancelButton` on the run's row, and pressing `planCancelButton` records the cancel. `KitWindowTests` (steps 414-418): `the flow strip UiIds are the stable intent-named ids` also pins `FlowPlanStep`; `the flow strip shows Items, Setups and Experiments left of the surface its step shows` also finds, in the Inverse window, the Plan box between Unknowns and Fit and, on `PlanFlowStep`, `planPanel`, and in the Main window no Plan box; `a read-only window withholds every write control` finds `planRunButton` present in `planView` over the read-only model (a plan writes no kit file). `KitWindowModelTests` (steps 414-418): `the flow strip's steps follow 001's order and a window opens on Setups` lists Items, Setups, Experiments, Data, Unknowns, Plan, Fit, Results and Publish with their captions; `the Data step is the Inverse constructor's alone, and leaving the Inverse constructor leaves it` also finds `stepsOf ForwardConstructor` without Plan, `ShowFlowStep PlanFlowStep` over `initMain ()` changing nothing, and `SwitchConstructorMode ForwardConstructor` from `PlanFlowStep` answering `ExperimentsFlowStep`. `ScrollExtentTests` gains `the kit window's Plan step leaves everything reachable`: `assertReachable "KitWindowPlan"` (`ScrollExtentTests.fs:assertReachable`) over a `HostWindow` running `kitWindowView` over `planKitIn`'s model on `PlanFlowStep` with a completed plan and a running one (its `planJob` started through a test-local host and given one `PlanProgressed`).

**Acceptance.** After the Plan step lands, the Inverse constructor's flow strip MUST show Plan between Unknowns and Fit and the Main constructor's none, and `planView` MUST offer the study's crystal materials, the two criteria and Run plan with per-candidate progress and Cancel on one row, and show the committed report's findings, rank, confounded combinations, bounds and instrument choices under their `ConstructorUiId`s; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including the changed `the flow strip's steps follow 001's order and a window opens on Setups` and `the Data step is the Inverse constructor's alone, and leaving the Inverse constructor leaves it`; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `pressing Run plan starts one plan through the shell's host, and Cancel cancels it`, the count rising by 1; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the plan view UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`, `the Plan step shows a plan's findings, rank, confounded combinations, bounds and instrument choices` and `the kit window's Plan step leaves everything reachable`, the count rising by 3, and the changed `the flow strip UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`, `the flow strip shows Items, Setups and Experiments left of the surface its step shows` and `a read-only window withholds every write control`; and build, elevation and the twenty-one s46 invariants MUST pass.
